# Day 32

**16km / 4 hours**

The day began with the morning fog lingering in the air, the cooling clouds whispering to us about the day to come. That sounds dramatic but the day was fairly mundane, just featuring road walking and some farm walking next to the river. 

![The Waikato River in the gloomy fog obscuring its size](./river-fog.jpg)

The only real landmark of note is probably the Huntly power station which you pass on the way in to the town. It's an impressive building even it is antiquated, both in age and function given that it's burning fossil fuels. Apart from that, Huntly sure is a town; can pick up some supplies there but wouldn't want to stay too long.